member-sites.md: where the factory stands at the reboot
Notes for whoever arrives next, put in the repository rather than only in a
session record — you are changing the host label, so the sessions that follow
will be new rather than resumed and will have none of this in memory.

One section in `docs/member-sites.md`. No code.

## The one thing worth saying plainly

**The machinery is finished and has no users, and those two facts look identical
from outside.** `sites.yml` holds `site` and `site-template` and nothing else, so
every passing check is passing over an empty set. Nothing is broken; nobody is
listed.

That is the sentence a new session most needs, because the alternative reading —
that this is working and publishing — is available from every other signal in the
repository.

## What it records

**The next commit, and why it is that one.** The generated tier from #93: a show
without its own repository still gets a site, built from show data plus
`member-site-core/`. The arithmetic is the argument — `site/_shows/` holds 1 and
`site/_podcasts/` holds 8, so the first run produces nine sites against today's
zero, with no member doing anything.

**Its one undecided point**, flagged as wanting a decision *before* it is built:
a generated site has no repository and therefore no gitlink, so it is neither
`tenant` nor `listed`. Plus the rule that holds either way — it must never be
confusable with `scaffold`, because the template must never reach the public and
a generated site must always reach it.

**The decisions being held for you, marked as held rather than missing.** The
wildcard rewrite, the name of `member-site-core/`, the template's
audience-facing README, the shows/podcasts collapse, and the signal that should
replace the Thursday schedule. An agent arriving cold could reasonably mistake
any of those for an oversight and settle it; the table says not to.

**Two facts no tool reports.** `.advocate-engine` is pinned 5 commits behind
(`4635cfc1`) and a clean `git status` will never say so, because a superproject
is clean when the gitlink matches what was committed — a statement about the
commit, not about the world. And the live site is served from a personal
Cloudflare account via `new.fcpublicmedia.org` → `fcpm.autumn-e2c.workers.dev`.

